# Line-ending policy for the edge.
#
# thirdparty/ (picoquic, picotls) is vendored at exact upstream commits. Any
# normalization there would diff it away from those commits, including picotls's own
# native Windows project files. -text disables every line-ending handling for these
# paths, so a checkout and a checkin never touch a byte.
#
# This file exists because the rule used to live in native/gyreplane/.gitattributes.
# The vendored copies moved here with the transport, and the rule did not follow them.
# A git mv preserves the blob, so nothing was damaged. A later checkout on a host that
# writes CRLF would have been.
thirdparty/** -text

# Everything the edge owns: normalize to LF on checkin whatever a checkout produced, and
# check out as LF. This is a Linux and POSIX codebase.
*.c text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.cpp text eol=lf
*.hpp text eol=lf
*.cc text eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt text eol=lf
*.cmake text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# Binary, never subject to any text handling.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.bin binary
*.a binary
*.so binary
